Video Surveillance Policy  
• Provide guidance and support for the VSS and Digital Recordings; 
• Install and maintain VSS in accordance with this policy; 
• Respond to requests for disclosure made pursuant to 6.14 to 6.17of this 
policy; 
• Capture, retain, and arrange for the viewing, export, and/or distribution of 
Digital Recordings when required by this policy; 
• Maintain the security of Digital Recordings within their custody and control; 
5.6. Executive Directors and Senior Managers are responsible to: 
• Ensure that staff are aware of and abide by this Policy and any related 
procedures; 
• Ensure the appropriate use of the VSS at their facilities, where applicable; 
• Refer any external requests for Digital Recordings to the City Clerk. 
5.7. Employees are responsible to: 
• Follow this Policy and its related procedures in all circumstances; 
• Report to their Supervisor or Manager any suspected Privacy Breach; 
• Comply with retention periods applicable to Digital Recordings; 
• Maintain the security of Digital Recordings within their custody and control. 


6. GOVERNING RULES AND REGULATIONS 
6.1. This policy reflects the provisions of MFIPPA and is subject to MFIPPA and any 
other privacy legislation that may apply in the circumstances.  To the extent that 
this policy may conflict with applicable privacy legislation, the applica ble privacy 
legislation shall prevail. 
6.2. By-law 21-2013, Records Retention By-law. 
6.3. To the extent that this policy may conflict with an applicable collective agreement, 
the applicable collective agreement shall prevail.

Video Surveillance Policy  
